            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-47764",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-47764: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-47764?s=github&n=cookie&t=npm&vr=%3C0.7.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "### Impact\n\nThe cookie name could be used to set other fields of the cookie, resulting in an unexpected cookie value. For example, `serialize(\"userName=<script>alert('XSS3')</script>; Max-Age=2592000; a\", value)` would result in `\"userName=<script>alert('XSS3')</script>; Max-Age=2592000; a=test\"`, setting `userName` cookie to `<script>` and ignoring `value`.\n\nA similar escape can be used for `path` and `domain`, which could be abused to alter other fields of the cookie.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to 0.7.0, which updates the validation for `name`, `path`, and `domain`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nAvoid passing untrusted or arbitrary values for these fields, ensure they are set by the application instead of user input.\n\n### References\n\n* https://github.com/jshttp/cookie/pull/167\n",
                "markdown": "> ### Impact\n\nThe cookie name could be used to set other fields of the cookie, resulting in an unexpected cookie value. For example, `serialize(\"userName=<script>alert('XSS3')</script>; Max-Age=2592000; a\", value)` would result in `\"userName=<script>alert('XSS3')</script>; Max-Age=2592000; a=test\"`, setting `userName` cookie to `<script>` and ignoring `value`.\n\nA similar escape can be used for `path` and `domain`, which could be abused to alter other fields of the cookie.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to 0.7.0, which updates the validation for `name`, `path`, and `domain`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nAvoid passing untrusted or arbitrary values for these fields, ensure they are set by the application instead of user input.\n\n### References\n\n* https://github.com/jshttp/cookie/pull/167\n\n|                                      |\n|Package         pkg:npm/cookie@0.4.2  |\n|Affected range  <0.7.0                |\n|Fixed version   0.7.0                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<0.7.0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "0.7.0",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/cookie@0.4.2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3449",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-3449: Incorrect Control Flow Scoping"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-3449?s=github&n=once&ns=%40tootallnate&t=npm&vr=%3C2.0.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Versions of the package @tootallnate/once before 3.0.1 are vulnerable to Incorrect Control Flow Scoping in promise resolving when AbortSignal option is used. The Promise remains in a permanently pending state after the signal is aborted, causing any await or .then() usage to hang indefinitely. This can cause a control-flow leak that can lead to stalled requests, blocked workers, or degraded application availability.\n",
                "markdown": "> Versions of the package @tootallnate/once before 3.0.1 are vulnerable to Incorrect Control Flow Scoping in promise resolving when AbortSignal option is used. The Promise remains in a permanently pending state after the signal is aborted, causing any await or .then() usage to hang indefinitely. This can cause a control-flow leak that can lead to stalled requests, blocked workers, or degraded application availability.\n\n|                                                                                                                                         |\n|Package                                                                                               pkg:npm/%40tootallnate/once@1.1.2  |\n|Affected range                                                                                        <2.0.1                             |\n|Fixed version                                                                                         3.0.1                              |\n|[[CVSS Score 1.9] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P]]                                     |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.0.1",
                "cvssV3": 1.9,
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P",
                "fixed_version": "3.0.1",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/%40tootallnate/once@1.1.2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "1.9",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-14505",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-14505: Use of a Cryptographic Primitive with a Risky Implementation"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-14505?s=github&n=elliptic&t=npm&vr=%3C%3D6.6.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "The ECDSA implementation of the Elliptic package generates incorrect signatures if an interim value of 'k' (as computed based on step 3.2 of  RFC 6979 https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6979 ) has leading zeros and is susceptible to cryptanalysis, which can lead to secret key exposure. This happens, because the byte-length of 'k' is incorrectly computed, resulting in its getting truncated during the computation. Legitimate transactions or communications will be broken as a result. Furthermore, due to the nature of the fault, attackers could–under certain conditions–derive the secret key, if they could get their hands on both a faulty signature generated by a vulnerable version of Elliptic and a correct signature for the same inputs.\n\nThis issue affects all known versions of Elliptic (at the time of writing, versions less than or equal to 6.6.1).\n",
                "markdown": "> The ECDSA implementation of the Elliptic package generates incorrect signatures if an interim value of 'k' (as computed based on step 3.2 of  RFC 6979 https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6979 ) has leading zeros and is susceptible to cryptanalysis, which can lead to secret key exposure. This happens, because the byte-length of 'k' is incorrectly computed, resulting in its getting truncated during the computation. Legitimate transactions or communications will be broken as a result. Furthermore, due to the nature of the fault, attackers could–under certain conditions–derive the secret key, if they could get their hands on both a faulty signature generated by a vulnerable version of Elliptic and a correct signature for the same inputs.\n\nThis issue affects all known versions of Elliptic (at the time of writing, versions less than or equal to 6.6.1).\n\n|                                                                                                                              |\n|Package                                                                                               pkg:npm/elliptic@6.6.1  |\n|Affected range                                                                                        <=6.6.1                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                                         not fixed               |\n|[[CVSS Score 2.9] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P]]                          |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<=6.6.1",
                "cvssV3": 2.9,
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/elliptic@6.6.1"
                ],
                "security-severity": "2.9",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-16016",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-16016: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2017-16016?s=github&n=sanitize-html&t=npm&vr=%3C%3D1.11.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Affected versions of `sanitize-html` are vulnerable to cross-site scripting when allowedTags includes at least one `nonTextTag`.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\n```js\nvar sanitizeHtml = require('sanitize-html');\n\nvar dirty = '!<textarea>&lt;/textarea&gt;<svg/onload=prompt`xs`&gt;</textarea>!';\nvar clean = sanitizeHtml(dirty, {\n    allowedTags: [ 'textarea' ]\n});\n\nconsole.log(clean);\n\n// !<textarea></textarea><svg/onload=prompt`xs`></textarea>!\n```\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 1.11.4 or later.\n",
                "markdown": "> Affected versions of `sanitize-html` are vulnerable to cross-site scripting when allowedTags includes at least one `nonTextTag`.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\n```js\nvar sanitizeHtml = require('sanitize-html');\n\nvar dirty = '!<textarea>&lt;/textarea&gt;<svg/onload=prompt`xs`&gt;</textarea>!';\nvar clean = sanitizeHtml(dirty, {\n    allowedTags: [ 'textarea' ]\n});\n\nconsole.log(clean);\n\n// !<textarea></textarea><svg/onload=prompt`xs`></textarea>!\n```\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 1.11.4 or later.\n\n|                                             |\n|Package         pkg:npm/sanitize-html@1.4.2  |\n|Affected range  <=1.11.1                     |\n|Fixed version   1.11.4                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<=1.11.1",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "1.11.4",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/sanitize-html@1.4.2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.1",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-rvg8-pwq2-xj7q",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GHSA-rvg8-pwq2-xj7q: Out-of-bounds Read"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/GHSA-rvg8-pwq2-xj7q?s=github&n=base64url&t=npm&vr=%3C3.0.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Versions of `base64url` before 3.0.0 are vulnerable to to out-of-bounds reads as it allocates uninitialized Buffers when number is passed in input on Node.js 4.x and below.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 3.0.0 or later.\n",
                "markdown": "> Versions of `base64url` before 3.0.0 are vulnerable to to out-of-bounds reads as it allocates uninitialized Buffers when number is passed in input on Node.js 4.x and below.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 3.0.0 or later.\n\n|                                         |\n|Package         pkg:npm/base64url@0.0.6  |\n|Affected range  <3.0.0                   |\n|Fixed version   3.0.0                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<3.0.0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "3.0.0",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/base64url@0.0.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.1",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-45736",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-45736: Use of Uninitialized Resource"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-45736?s=github&n=ws&t=npm&vr=%3E%3D8.0.0%2C%3C8.20.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "### Impact\n\nThe `websocket.close()` implementation is vulnerable to uninitialized memory disclosure when a `TypedArray` is passed as the reason argument.\n\n### Proof of concept\n\n```js\nimport { deepStrictEqual } from 'node:assert';\nimport { WebSocket, WebSocketServer } from 'ws';\n\nconst wss = new WebSocketServer(\n  { port: 0, skipUTF8Validation: true },\n  function () {\n    const { port } = wss.address();\n    const ws = new WebSocket(`ws://localhost:${port}`, {\n      skipUTF8Validation: true\n    });\n\n    ws.on('close', function (code, reason) {\n      deepStrictEqual(reason, Buffer.alloc(80));\n    });\n  }\n);\n\nwss.on('connection', function (ws) {\n  ws.close(1000, new Float32Array(20));\n});\n```\n\n### Patches\n\nThe vulnerability was fixed in ws@8.20.1 (https://github.com/websockets/ws/commit/c0327ec15a54d701eb6ccefaa8bef328cfc03086).\n\n### Credits\n\nCredit for the private and responsible disclosure of this issue goes to [Nikita Skovoroda](https://github.com/ChALkeR).\n\n### Remarks\n\nAlthough the calculated CVSS severity is medium, the actual severity is believed to be low, as the flaw is only exploitable through misuse that is unlikely in practice.\n\n### Resources\n\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-58qx-3vcg-4xpx\n- https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-45736\n",
                "markdown": "> ### Impact\n\nThe `websocket.close()` implementation is vulnerable to uninitialized memory disclosure when a `TypedArray` is passed as the reason argument.\n\n### Proof of concept\n\n```js\nimport { deepStrictEqual } from 'node:assert';\nimport { WebSocket, WebSocketServer } from 'ws';\n\nconst wss = new WebSocketServer(\n  { port: 0, skipUTF8Validation: true },\n  function () {\n    const { port } = wss.address();\n    const ws = new WebSocket(`ws://localhost:${port}`, {\n      skipUTF8Validation: true\n    });\n\n    ws.on('close', function (code, reason) {\n      deepStrictEqual(reason, Buffer.alloc(80));\n    });\n  }\n);\n\nwss.on('connection', function (ws) {\n  ws.close(1000, new Float32Array(20));\n});\n```\n\n### Patches\n\nThe vulnerability was fixed in ws@8.20.1 (https://github.com/websockets/ws/commit/c0327ec15a54d701eb6ccefaa8bef328cfc03086).\n\n### Credits\n\nCredit for the private and responsible disclosure of this issue goes to [Nikita Skovoroda](https://github.com/ChALkeR).\n\n### Remarks\n\nAlthough the calculated CVSS severity is medium, the actual severity is believed to be low, as the flaw is only exploitable through misuse that is unlikely in practice.\n\n### Resources\n\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-58qx-3vcg-4xpx\n- https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-45736\n\n|                                                                                                  |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:npm/ws@8.17.1  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=8.0.0,<8.20.1    |\n|Fixed version                                                                  8.20.1             |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.4] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                     |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=8.0.0,<8.20.1",
                "cvssV3": 4.4,
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N",
                "fixed_version": "8.20.1",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/ws@8.17.1",
                  "pkg:npm/ws@8.18.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.4",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-29425",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-29425: Improper Input Validation"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2021-29425?s=github&n=commons-io&ns=commons-io&t=maven&vr=%3C2.7",
              "help": {
                "text": "In Apache Commons IO before 2.7, When invoking the method FileNameUtils.normalize with an improper input string, like \"//../foo\", or \"\\\\..\\foo\", the result would be the same value, thus possibly providing access to files in the parent directory, but not further above (thus \"limited\" path traversal), if the calling code would use the result to construct a path value.\n",
                "markdown": "> In Apache Commons IO before 2.7, When invoking the method FileNameUtils.normalize with an improper input string, like \"//../foo\", or \"\\\\..\\foo\", the result would be the same value, thus possibly providing access to files in the parent directory, but not further above (thus \"limited\" path traversal), if the calling code would use the result to construct a path value.\n\n|                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:maven/commons-io/commons-io@2.4  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <2.7                                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                  2.7                                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.8] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N]]                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.7",
                "cvssV3": 4.8,
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "fixed_version": "2.7",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:maven/commons-io/commons-io@2.4"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
